{
  "id": "update-c27ef405cc62",
  "date": "2026-10-15",
  "title": "Faster neighborhoods and easier placement",
  "summary": "Independent scene caching, persistent nighttime lighting, and item placement across city and street views.",
  "changes": [
    "Buildings, streets, purchased items, and public sites render from independent cached assets. Financial and profile updates preserve their geometry.",
    "Surface batching, spatial queries, reusable woodland tiles, bounded neighbor models, and background pathfinding reduce rendering and movement work.",
    "Every placed lamp and shop window keeps warm ambient ground illumination at night; nearby dynamic lights add detail with stable selection and smooth handoffs.",
    "Switch between City view and Street view while placing an item without losing its position, rotation, or purchase request.",
    "Local dev tools can populate the neighborhood with a dense repeat-safe fixture and grant custom brick amounts."
  ],
